# FLOWLAB - Docker build context exclusions.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT
# ---------------------------------------
# Docker reads exactly ONE ignore file per build: `<context root>/.dockerignore`.
# There is no recursive search, so a `backend/.dockerignore` is inert whenever
# the context is anything other than ./backend - which is why backend/.dockerignore
# sat unused while the whole checkout was uploaded.
#
# Two builds exist, and this file applies to only one of them:
#
#   1. the `backend` service: context `.`, dockerfile `backend/Dockerfile`.
#      THIS is the file Docker reads.  backend/Dockerfile needs, from the root:
#        frontend/package.json      - node stage, `npm ci` layer
#        frontend/package-lock.json - ditto; without it `npm ci` fails
#        frontend/**                - `COPY frontend/ ./`, then `npm run build`
#        backend/requirements.txt   - `COPY ... ; pip install -r`
#        backend/**                 - `COPY backend ./backend` (the app + demo JSON)
#        README.md                  - `COPY README.md ./`
#      Nothing below may exclude any of those paths.
#
#   2. the `frontend` dev service: context `./frontend`, dockerfile `Dockerfile`.
#      Its context root is frontend/, so Docker reads frontend/.dockerignore and
#      NOT this file.  The dev image is unaffected by anything here.
#
# Docker is not installed on the machine this file was written on, so this list
# is justified by reading both Dockerfiles rather than by a successful build.
# Re-verify with `docker compose build backend` after changing it.
#
# Later patterns win, so a negation always comes after the rule it undoes.

# --- never ship a virtualenv -----------------------------------------------
# An empty or half-built .venv is still megabytes of irrelevant context.
.venv
**/.venv
venv
**/venv

# --- node ------------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- git -------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
**/.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- local data and weights ------------------------------------------------
# uploads, annotated videos, the SQLite database and the YOLO checkpoint are
# all host state; the image downloads the checkpoint on first use.
data
**/data
*.pt
**/*.pt
models

# --- python build artefacts -------------------------------------------------
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.pyd
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info

# --- frontend build output --------------------------------------------------
# The backend image builds dist inside the node stage and copies it from
# there; a stale host dist in the context only masks that build.
frontend/dist
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- repository furniture ---------------------------------------------------
.kilo
.idea
.vscode
.editorconfig
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.github
docs
run.bat
run.sh
docker-compose.yml
pyproject.toml
CONTRIBUTING.md
*.log
**/*.log

# Not needed to serve the API, and nothing in the runtime import graph reaches
# them (only backend/tests imports backend/scripts).
backend/tests
backend/scripts
backend/validation
backend/Dockerfile
backend/.dockerignore

# KEEP: `COPY README.md ./` in backend/Dockerfile fails without this line, and
# it is listed last because later patterns win, which is what keeps it working
# if a broad `*.md` is ever added above.
!README.md
